insert into public.manual_chapters (slug, part, position, number_label, title, subtitle, truth, confidentiality, draft_status, pull_quote, provenance_note, body) values
('from-license-to-tournament','saga',101,'Chapter 101','From the License to the Tournament','Act 3 opens: the offer that no one could name','HYPOTHESIS','C1','drafting',
'What is my offer? Does anyone know? Can anyone assume or predict?',
'Written 2026-10-10 from founder sessions of 2026-10-08 to 10. Outside model readings (Grok, ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude) were priming material only; the founder will supply the clean narrative. Ruling: ADR-039. Register: A142.',
$md$Act 2 ended with a seat. Chapter 99 framed the Personal Seat License as one Door, one seat, one number, and the outside readings of the seed deck pushed that seat to its logical edge: ten seats at ten million dollars for ten percent, so that one sale marks the whole network at a billion. That arithmetic is SIMULATION. It is also a different number from the ten-million-dollar assigned-value baseline in ADR-034, and the two were written against different calendars. The ambiguity is itself the finding.

The founder then asked the question that opens Act 3: what is my offer, and can anyone predict it? The honest answer, recorded here as FACT about the corpus, is no. No price, quota, territory or seat has been approved anywhere in these documents.

So the founder turned the question over. What if the first thing offered is not a license at all, but a contest? Whoever originates the most revenue, the most Property Owners, the most ISRs, Licensed Contractors and adjusting professionals; the most leads; the most project revenue. What if we sell tickets instead of seats?

That is held as HYPOTHESIS. A ticket asks for a smaller act than a license, invites voluntary entry, and does not ask anyone to believe a valuation before the scoreboard has produced one. The PSL is not abandoned. It is held, and Chapters 98 and 99 stand as written. Predict small still governs: any ticket, prize or qualifier is tested against one season and one Door before it is generalized, and no money is modeled ahead of its gate.$md$),
('national-roofing-league','saga',102,'Chapter 102','The National Roofing League','A scoreboard we already own','HYPOTHESIS','C1','drafting',
'Not round robin. I want my leads going to the top closer, seller, quality contractor.',
'Written 2026-10-10. ClaimExpress ranking history and the current codebase ranking are founder ASSERTION pending inspection (see A113). Register: A143.',
$md$The founder bought the National Roofing League domain knowing the scorekeeping already existed. The original ClaimExpress platform ranked ISRs and Licensed Contractors by project volume, and the founder states the current codebase does the same. That ranking extends naturally to self-generated leads, offers completed, closing percentage and Task Efficiency Rating.

These are not game rules first. They are the rules anyone running SiteBMS needs to assign work. Round-robin distribution treats the best closer and the weakest one as interchangeable; the founder rejects that outright. Work goes to demonstrated performance. The League is that same rule made visible as a season.

Several boundaries hold. TER remains private, rank versus average, never public and never sold (ADR-015 and memory); a public standing must be built from other metrics or from consented display. Lead assignment rules belong to SiteBMS and wait on the Records gate. Targeting methods behind any lead source stay in Band 3. Season 1 is aimed at Super Bowl Weekend, February 11 to 14, 2027 — a direction, not a published commitment.

The launch posture the founder chose is simple: lead publicly with Kimosabe.AI, the Kimosabe Commons and the National Roofing League. PrepareAmerica's mission, RRCA and Adjusting Professionals stay under the table and invite-only while the rhetoric is perfected, so interest builds without confusion.$md$),
('the-vault-and-the-arena','saga',103,'Chapter 103','The Vault and the Arena','Two projects, one record, and the airlock between them','DECISION','C1','drafting',
'The fork has already been done.',
'Written 2026-10-10. The remix was executed by the founder (FACT, founder statement); setup of the new project is pending founder steps. Ruling: ADR-039. Register: A144.',
$md$On October 10 the founder confirmed the remix: a second project now exists beside this one. That is the structural act of Act 3, and it is recorded as a DECISION.

This project is the Vault. It holds the corpus, the Manual, the decisions and register, the Connecticut Agreement work, the Records and SiteBMS path, JobNimbus mapping, and the invite-only institutional Doors — PrepareAmerica, RRCA and Adjusting Professionals. Its standing rule does not change: if it is not in the corpus, it did not happen.

The remix is the Arena. It is the public launch surface for Kimosabe.AI, the Kimosabe Commons and the National Roofing League. It speaks to the market; it does not hold the canon.

Between them sits an airlock. Nothing crosses by inference. Doctrine moves from Vault to Arena only as written copy cleared to its confidentiality class; nothing moves from Arena to Vault except as recorded evidence. Any shared record, API or event sync waits for the Records / Object Model gate and then the API gate — the locked work order is unchanged. The Arena carries no Band 3 method, no capital intake, and no claims the Vault has not cleared.

What stays OPEN: whether the Arena's backend ever shares data with the Vault, who operates it, and what the Arena's first ticket or prize is. Those return to the founder.$md$);

